details.image_prompt:
[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. Composition and framing: Two round, matte ceramic bowls are centered in the frame, angled at 35-45 degrees to clearly display the contents. One bowl is in sharp focus in the foreground, with the second bowl slightly blurred in the background. Generous negative space around the bowls. Lighting: Soft natural side light streaming from a window to the left, casting gentle, natural shadows and creating a slight sheen on the moist surface of the oatmeal. Setting and styling: The bowls sit on a rustic, weathered oak wooden surface with visible grain. Props include a tarnished silver spoon resting casually on the linen tablecloth beside the bowl and a few loose, scattered walnut fragments and a single stray raspberry on the wood surface. The oatmeal is thick and creamy with a slightly airy, fluffy texture from the egg whites, displaying a soft beige color with warm cinnamon flecks. The mixed berries—blueberries and raspberries—are partially thawed, creating streaks of deep violet and bright crimson swirls throughout the porridge. Chopped walnuts are sprinkled generously over the top of each serving. Realism and anti-AI: Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene appears lived-in and authentic, as if just prepared in a home kitchen. Subtle imperfections include a slight smudge of berry juice on the side of one bowl, uneven distribution of the chopped nuts, and a few stray crumbs on the oak table. The color temperature is warm and golden-hour cozy. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no artificial lighting, no text, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography for a high-end cookbook."
  }
]
